.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dnglab-process-raw 1  "dnglab-process-raw " 
.SH NAME
dnglab\-process\-raw
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdnglab\-process\-raw\fR [\fB\-\-remove\-dng\-opcodes\fR] [\fB\-\-bad\-pixels\fR] [\fB\-\-artist\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-mtime\fR] [\fB\-\-image\-index\fR] [\fB\-\-crop\fR] [\fB\-\-crop\-transparent\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-color\-space\fR] [\fB\-\-highlights\fR] [\fB\-\-dcp\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-jpeg\-quality\fR] [\fB\-\-denoise\-luma\fR] [\fB\-\-denoise\-chroma\fR] [\fB\-\-sharpen\fR] [\fB\-\-exposure\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-exposure\fR] [\fB\-\-steps\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-steps\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-override\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-recursive\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-dng\-opcodes\fR \fI<opcodes>\fR
Remove DNG opcodes, as comma separated [<list>:]<opcode> (e.g. WarpRectilinear,2:GainMap)
.TP
\fB\-\-bad\-pixels\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Bad pixel list in the format of dcraw: column, row and UNIX time per line, relative to the ActiveArea. It is written as FixBadPixelsList to OpcodeList1 and replaces an existing one
.TP
\fB\-\-artist\fR \fI<artist>\fR
Set the artist tag
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-mtime\fR \fI<keepmtime>\fR [default: false]
Keep mtime, read from EXIF with fallback to original file mtime
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-image\-index\fR \fI<index>\fR [default: 0]
Select a specific image index (or \*(Aqall\*(Aq) if file is a image container
.TP
\fB\-\-crop\fR \fI<crop>\fR [default: best]
Crop of the image: DefaultCrop (best), ActiveArea or none
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
best
.IP \(bu 2
activearea
.IP \(bu 2
none
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-crop\-transparent\fR
Crop to the largest rectangle without transparent pixels of the DNG transparency mask
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output image format, defaults to the OUTPUT file extension or tif. TIFF has 16\-bit samples, linear 32\-bit floating point samples for High Dynamic Range camera profiles
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
tif
.IP \(bu 2
jpeg
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\-space\fR \fI<space>\fR [default: srgb]
Color space of the image
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
srgb
.IP \(bu 2
adobergb
.IP \(bu 2
prophoto
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-highlights\fR \fI<mode>\fR [default: compress]
Highlights above white after the BaselineExposure: compress keeps their color with a smooth shoulder, clip clips each channel like DNG readers
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
compress
.IP \(bu 2
clip
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dcp\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Camera profile (DCP) to render the image with, replaces the primary camera profile
.TP
\fB\-\-jpeg\-quality\fR \fI<quality>\fR [default: 94]
JPEG quality (1\-100)
.TP
\fB\-\-denoise\-luma\fR \fI<strength>\fR
Strength of the luma noise reduction (0\-4), 0 is off, 1 is a full reduction [default: 0.25]
.TP
\fB\-\-denoise\-chroma\fR \fI<strength>\fR
Strength of the chroma noise reduction (0\-4), 0 is off, 1 is a full reduction [default: 0.5]
.TP
\fB\-\-sharpen\fR \fI<strength>\fR
Strength of the sharpening (0\-2), 0 is off, 1 is the classic Laplacian filter [default: 0.2]
.TP
\fB\-\-exposure\fR \fI<EV>\fR
Change the exposure by this value in EV, e.g. \-1.2. A negative value keeps white [default: 0]
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-exposure\fR
Correct the exposure by an estimate from the image, \-\-exposure is added to it
.TP
\fB\-\-steps\fR \fI<steps>\fR
Apply only these processing steps of the rendering, as comma separated list. Without it the default steps are applied
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
rescale
.IP \(bu 2
demosaic
.IP \(bu 2
fujirotate
.IP \(bu 2
cropactivearea
.IP \(bu 2
baselineexposure
.IP \(bu 2
whitebalance
.IP \(bu 2
autowhitebalance
.IP \(bu 2
calibrate
.IP \(bu 2
profilerender
.IP \(bu 2
tonecurve
.IP \(bu 2
cropdefault
.IP \(bu 2
denoise
.IP \(bu 2
defaultscale
.IP \(bu 2
exposure
.IP \(bu 2
autoexposure
.IP \(bu 2
sharpen
.IP \(bu 2
transferfunction
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-steps\fR \fI<steps>\fR
Skip these processing steps of the rendering, as comma separated list (e.g. tonecurve,denoise,sharpen). Takes priority over \-\-steps
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
rescale
.IP \(bu 2
demosaic
.IP \(bu 2
fujirotate
.IP \(bu 2
cropactivearea
.IP \(bu 2
baselineexposure
.IP \(bu 2
whitebalance
.IP \(bu 2
autowhitebalance
.IP \(bu 2
calibrate
.IP \(bu 2
profilerender
.IP \(bu 2
tonecurve
.IP \(bu 2
cropdefault
.IP \(bu 2
denoise
.IP \(bu 2
defaultscale
.IP \(bu 2
exposure
.IP \(bu 2
autoexposure
.IP \(bu 2
sharpen
.IP \(bu 2
transferfunction
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-override\fR
Override existing files
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-recursive\fR
Process input directory recursive
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Input file or directory
.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>
Output file or existing directory
